    "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Fairbanks AK",
    "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued November 19 at 2:41AM AKST until November 19 at 3:00PM AKST by NWS Fairbanks AK",
    "description": "* WHAT...Water levels of 3 to 5 feet above the normal high tide\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Seward Peninsula Coast.\n\n* WHEN...Until 3 PM AKST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor coastal flooding is possible. In Nome, water\ncould approach homes in the Belmont Subdivision, portions of the\nport area will have standing water, and wave run-up will push\nwater higher than normal. In Golovin, water will approach beach\nproperty.",
    "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.",
    "response": "Monitor",
    "note": null,
